  "steps": [
    "Heat a large, high-sided frying pan over medium heat. Add the oil and onion with a pinch of salt and cook for 5 minutes until softened.",
    "Add the garlic, cumin and cinnamon and cook for 1 minute until fragrant.",
    "Add the lentils, chopped tomatoes and stock. Bring to the boil, then reduce to a simmer and cook for 20–25 minutes until the lentils are tender.",
    "Season well with lemon juice, salt and pepper. Serve scattered with mint leaves if you like."
  ],
  "notes": "Great with crusty bread or flatbread for mopping up. Leftovers thicken overnight — loosen with a splash of water when reheating."
}
